Subject: [PATCH] (optional hardening) naive_sdpa: compute attention scores in F32

OPTIONAL, defense-in-depth. Patch 0001 already fixes the reported Qwen3-14B NaN
by never auto-selecting F16 on non-CUDA devices. This additionally makes the
eager attention path safe even if F16 is forced explicitly.

NOTE: This does NOT cover the Metal prefill path, which uses the fused kernel
candle_nn::ops::sdpa (see attention/mod.rs::run_attention_noflash), not
naive_sdpa. Only patch 0001 fixes Metal. Apply 0001 regardless.

The current code upcasts to F32 for the softmax, but only AFTER the F16 Q*K^T
matmul -- by then an overflowed score is already Inf. Upcasting Q/K before the
matmul keeps scores finite. The score matrix is small relative to the weights.

--- a/mistralrs-core/src/attention/backends/naive.rs
+++ b/mistralrs-core/src/attention/backends/naive.rs
@@ -32,8 +32,16 @@
 
     // Use chunked attention with a closure that captures the necessary parameters
     chunked_attention(q, k, v, mask, |q_chunk, k, v, mask_chunk| {
+        // Compute attention scores in F32 to avoid F16 overflow: a large Q*K^T
+        // entry can exceed F16's 65504 maximum, become Inf, and then NaN after
+        // softmax (seen with large models such as Qwen3-14B). Upcasting Q/K
+        // before the matmul keeps the scores finite. The score matrix is small
+        // relative to the weights, so the cost is minor.
+        let in_dtype = q_chunk.dtype();
+        let q_chunk = q_chunk.to_dtype(candle_core::DType::F32)?;
+        let k = k.to_dtype(candle_core::DType::F32)?;
         let mut att =
-            MatMul.matmul_affine_mul(q_chunk, &k.t()?, sdpa_params.softmax_scale.into())?;
+            MatMul.matmul_affine_mul(&q_chunk, &k.t()?, sdpa_params.softmax_scale.into())?;
 
         if let Some(softcap) = sdpa_params.softcap {
             att = (att / softcap as f64)?;
@@ -42,17 +50,15 @@
         }
 
         if let Some(mask) = mask_chunk {
-            att = att.broadcast_add(mask)?;
+            att = att.broadcast_add(&mask.to_dtype(candle_core::DType::F32)?)?;
         }
 
-        // Compute softmax in F32 for precision (BF16 exp() loses information).
-        let att_dtype = att.dtype();
-        if att_dtype == candle_core::DType::BF16 || att_dtype == candle_core::DType::F16 {
-            att = att.to_dtype(candle_core::DType::F32)?;
-        }
+        // Scores are already F32 here; softmax stays in F32 for precision.
         att = candle_nn::ops::softmax_last_dim(&att)?;
-        if att.dtype() != att_dtype {
-            att = att.to_dtype(att_dtype)?;
+        // Cast the (bounded, in [0,1]) probabilities back to the compute dtype
+        // for the att @ V matmul.
+        if att.dtype() != in_dtype {
+            att = att.to_dtype(in_dtype)?;
         }
         MatMul.matmul(&att, v)
     })
